  "decision": "REVIEW",
  "executive_summary": "Tag v2.2.0 (268ba643) is version-consistent (pyproject, package __version__, GitHub release) and CI on the tag succeeded. Release is blocked from a clean GO by an undocumented required SMTP_HOST that is read at import with no default; README and .env.example omit it while CI injects it, so tests stay green without covering startup config. Operators following published docs will crash on KeyError. Address docs/example env (and ideally a config test) before treating this as production-ready.",
